From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_JIT_REGALLOC_BITS=1: dynarmic x64 RegAlloc tracks changed and occupied locations in bitmasks instead of scanning all 102 (Lichii PR #1517); off by default

Port of zortos293/Lichii commit 8ddb4b9a386729f62496de630925b4acca168181 (PR #1517, "dynarmic:
RegAlloc tracks slots in bitmasks instead of scanning all 102"), by Zortos, co-authored by Liomar
Oliveira, GPL-3.0-or-later. Upstream measured JIT compile time -27%.

What upstream found: after every IR instruction EndOfAllocScope looks at all 102 host locations
(16 GPR, 16 XMM, 6 flags, 64 spill slots), every value lookup (ValueLocation, used by
GetArgumentInfo, IsValueLive, DefineValue) scans them in order, the spill-slot search walks the 64
spill slots, and each block constructs the allocator again (5.7 KB zeroed). With bitmasks of the
locations changed since the last scope end (dirty) and of those holding values (occupied), each of
these visits only the few locations that matter, and a block start zeroes only what changed.

Here (core only): the masks are kept in both modes (a few ORs per allocation, never read with the
switch off); the switch picks which code reads them.
- EDEN_UP_JIT_REGALLOC_BITS, exact "1" (Common::PeSwitch), read once at the first block, after
  env.txt, as EDEN_UP_JIT_COLD_CHUNKS. Unset: the emitters construct the allocator as before and
  EndOfAllocScope, ValueLocation, FindFreeSpill and AssertNoMoreUses run T181's scans; every
  allocation decision and the emitted code are T181's.
- On: RegAlloc::Reset instead of the placement new; the scope end releases only dirty locations;
  ValueLocation visits occupied ones in the same ascending order; FindFreeSpill takes the lowest
  spill slot without values.
- Why the output is the same with it on (same IR -> same code): a location is changed only by a
  lock (Read/WriteLock: the six lock sites mark it), an argument reference (both sites mark it), a
  new value (DefineValueImpl marks it), Move (marks the target; the source becomes a new empty
  one) or Exchange (marks both); ReleaseOne through Release only follows a lock in the same
  instruction. So at each scope end every location outside the dirty set is still in the released
  state the previous scope end left it in, and upstream's `if (!IsReleased()) ReleaseAll()` would
  not change it. Values appear only through AddValue, Move and Exchange and disappear only through
  ReleaseAll (scope end or Release) and Move's source; each of those updates the occupied bit, so
  it equals "values not empty" exactly, ValueLocation finds the same first match, and FindFreeSpill
  finds the same first empty spill slot (spill slots are never locked, so IsEmpty there is "no
  values"). A released, empty location equals a new one except lru_counter (when values clear,
  ReleaseAll zeroes the use counts and width), so Reset zeroes lru_counter only on locations that
  can hold a non-zero one.
- Differences from upstream: upstream's touched mask covers registers only; here every target of a
  Move or Exchange is marked too (a spill slot that took a register's lru_counter and was later
  emptied by ReleaseAll would otherwise keep it into the next block and pass it back to a
  register); Reset rebuilds all locations when a block did not end clean (any occupied or dirty
  bit left), where upstream relies on a debug assert; upstream removed the constructor, here it
  stays for the switch-off path. Upstream is always on.
- The front's reg_alloc.cmake still finds "if (!iter.IsReleased())" in reg_alloc.h and takes its
  codegen-only rewrite (MoveOutOfTheWay's free moves, R13 in SelectARegister); both of its anchors
  are unchanged. Its free-move path moves through Move, so it keeps the masks right.
- Log: "EDEN_UP_JIT_REGALLOC_BITS on=1" once at the first block; "EDEN_UP_JIT_REGALLOC_BITS
  blocks=N full_resets=M" every 65536 blocks over all emitters (full_resets should stay 0).

Store: dynarmic is not a translation id input and no name is added to TranslationSwitches:
KEEPS THE STORE.

